meta {
  name: Vendor Payout
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/payment-gateway/vendor/payout
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{accessToken}}
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "amount": "10",
    "vpaId": {{vendorVpaId}},
    "isTripExpense": false,
    "truckId": {{truckId}},
    "narration": "Vendor payment"
  }
}

docs {
  Pays a vendor's UPI ID from the caller's own VAHN wallet (`PaymentGatewayService.vendorPayout`).
  Get `vpaId` from `vpas/vendor-lookup` first. Only `@Authenticated`: there is no role or torg
  ownership check on the VPA or truck (logged as an open problem).

  Body: `amount` (string or number, > 0), `vpaId` (required), `isTripExpense` (null = false),
  `truckId` and `driverId` (optional, independent of one another; add `"driverId": <id>` to pin
  one), `narration` (optional; default
  "Vendor expense for trip <n>" or "Vendor payout").

  What happens, in order:
  1. A VENDOR transaction is recorded against the truck's in-progress trip, after the
     VENDOR_ACCOUNT spend-limit check (per truck, rolling 24h). With `isTripExpense: true` an
     OTHER_CHARGES "Vendor Payment" trip expense is raised on that trip.
  2. The wallet is debited and a RazorpayX payout is created. The `TXN-…` reference is sent as
     the RazorpayX idempotency key (PR #998), so a retried call cannot pay twice.
  3. A synchronous failure marks the transaction FAILED, removes the trip expense and refunds the
     wallet. Otherwise the final status arrives by webhook (staging never receives them).

  Response (captured on staging 2026-10-06; `amount` is net of charge-inclusive payout fees):

  {
    "success": true,
    "message": "Success",
    "statusCode": 200,
    "data": {
      "transactionId": "TXN-94992EEF",
      "entityId": 34277,
      "status": "PROCESSING",
      "amount": 8.230,
      "success": true
    }
  }

  Errors come back as HTTP 200 with `success:false` and `statusCode:400`, e.g. "Invalid amount",
  "VPA not found", or a spend-limit message. The same amount to the same UPI ID within ~30s is
  refused as a duplicate (HTTP 409). A missing `vpaId` returns `success:true` with
  `data.status: "FAILED"` (pre-existing quirk).
}
